{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a8f5e2c1-74b9-4d3e-9a12-6c8b0f4e9d21",
    "name": "RabbitLens Backend API (Runner Suite)",
    "description": "Automated Postman Collection Runner suite for testing every endpoint in the RabbitLens FastAPI Backend.\n\n### How to Run in Postman Collection Runner\n1. Import `RabbitLens_API.postman_collection.json` into Postman.\n2. For file upload steps (`12. Upload Rabbit Profile Photo`, `13. Process Paw Scan`, `18. Upload File`, `19. Azure ML Predict`), either:\n   - Copy `test_paw.jpg` into your **Postman Working Directory** (Settings -> General -> Working Directory), or\n   - Select `test_paw.jpg` in the Body tab of those requests.\n3. Click **Run collection** -> **Run RabbitLens Backend API (Runner Suite)**.\n\nEvery request includes automated `pm.test()` assertions and chains variables (`access_token`, `refresh_token`, `rabbit_id`, `photo_id`, `media_path`) automatically.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{access_token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8000",
      "type": "string"
    },
